meta {
  name: Patient Snapshot
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/apis/{{site}}/api/copilot/snapshot
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "patient_uuid": "{{patientUuid}}"
  }
}

docs {
  # Patient Snapshot

  `POST /api/copilot/snapshot` — the glanceable orientation snapshot the
  SMART-launched panel renders on arrival (founder call 2026-07-16): the
  code-detected must-not-miss findings, the new-labs-since-last-visit
  delta, current medications and allergies, honest unevaluable and
  unknown-currency lists, and the earned-quiet flag, all composed from ONE
  live chart read as the delegated physician (S4/S6; D9 one-pass
  synthesis). No LLM runs on this route.

  Requires the `user/snapshot.write` scope (deliberately "write", not
  "read" — the core dispatcher derives a POST's required action as
  `create`; identical constraint and rationale as the Source Resolve
  route) and the `patients`/`med` ACL.

  In a SMART-launched session the token's launch-context patient binds
  the request (TRO-52): a `patient_uuid` for anyone else is refused with
  a generic 403 before any chart read — neither uuid is echoed.

  Every entry's `refs[].token` is click-to-source: resolve it via
  `POST /api/copilot/source` (see Source Resolve) — a document-extracted
  lab resolves through its extraction lineage to the source PDF with the
  stored bounding box for the overlay.
}
